WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:04.037
-[ Gasps ]
-What?!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.595
-[ Gasps ]
It did it, babe!

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.333
-Ooh!

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:46.646
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.883
♪♪
-♪ We in the house ♪

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.250
-Come on!

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.586
-Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests...

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.092
Musical guest...

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:02.595
And the legendary Roots crew.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.430
It's "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.499
-♪ We in the house, y'all ♪

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.735
-And now, here's Jimmy.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.204
-Hi, everybody, and welcome to

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.872
"The Tonight Show: At Home
Edition."

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.073
My name's Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.008
Thank you so much
for watching our show tonight.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.143
Let's get to some jokes.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.912
Well, guys, everybody is
talking about this.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:21.347
This is insane.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.148
Last night, President Trump
claimed that

00:01:23.148 --> 00:01:26.152
he's been taking
hydroxychloroquine

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.521
to prevent himself from getting
the coronavirus.

00:01:29.521 --> 00:01:32.459
When told the drug is for
treating malaria, Trump said,

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.625
"If it's good enough for
the First Lady,

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:36.129
it's good enough for me."

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.430
That's right -- Trump shocked
everyone by saying

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.767
that he's taking the drug, even
though it has not been proven

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.535
to help treat COVID-19.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:45.371
Right after he said it,
Dr. Fauci immediately

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:48.541
put on a mask so no one
could see him laughing.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:52.778
[ Laughs ]

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:56.015
That's a little Muttley.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.416
Yeah, after Trump
made the announcement,

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:59.852
a lot of experts told him what
he was doing is dangerous.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.120
Trump was like, "Relax.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.788
if anything goes wrong,
I can just drink bleach

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.156
and clean it all out.

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.359
I'm good."

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:11.931
[ As Trump ] If you swallow a
U.V. light bulb, good as new.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.133
[ Normal voice ]
This is going viral.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.034
An Israeli company
has created a mask

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.003
that opens for you
to eat through.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.805
Oh, that's been a problem people
have been having.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.473
So, I guess when
you squeeze this thing,

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:23.175
it opens and closes
a mechanical mouth.

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:24.210
Take a look at this.

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:38.925
Yeah. It costs $19.99,
plus your dignity.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.359
It's actually made by
the same person

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:43.429
who invented
Steven Tyler's mouth.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.763
Listen to this.

00:02:44.763 --> 00:02:47.700
I saw that Michael Jordan
is selling his Chicago mansion

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.302
for almost $15 million.

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:52.672
It's a great place to live if
you've always dreamed of

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:56.041
disappointing the hell
out of trick-or-treaters.

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:57.976
Hmm.

00:02:57.976 --> 00:03:00.946
I heard about a priest in
Detroit who used a squirt gun

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:04.650
to shoot holy water onto his
churchgoers while they drove by.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.186
And after that,
he shot wafers into their mouths

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.821
from a T-shirt cannon.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.693
This is crazy.

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.796
Scientists in Antarctica
say that they've found evidence

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:20.199
of a parallel universe where
time actually runs backwards.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.467
Then they were like, "Oh, wait.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.904
We were just holding
the research the wrong way.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.906
Sorry."

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.207
And, finally,
I saw that researchers

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:29.808
are working on
a coronavirus test

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:32.545
where you sneeze onto
your phone.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.879
Sounds gross,
but I'd rather watch that

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:36.048
than someone eat that through
that mechanical mask.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:37.650
That is our monologue,
everybody.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.952
We have a great show tonight.
Oh, my goodness.

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:43.156
Ben Stiller is on the show.
I love Ben Stiller.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.256
I've known him for a while.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:45.992
You know, that was
my big "SNL" --

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.359
That was kind of my
big breakout show,

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:48.428
was the Ben Stiller show.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:50.029
-Right.
-Because of Ben.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.363
-He's done that
for a lot of people.

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:52.832
-He said -- Yeah.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.834
He said -- He goes, "Have you
heard this new kid, Sandler?"

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:55.901
And everyone was like,
"Yeah, we know.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:56.936
He auditioned.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:57.937
I mean, we hired him
for the show.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.071
We know who he is."

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.673
He's like, "You should have
him do Sandler."

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.075
They're like, "Yeah, we'll see.
He's brand-new."

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.178
This was only like my third show
or something like that.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.646
And he's like -- So, that night,

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:09.248
I did Sandler in
"Celebrity Jeopardy!"

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.684
and I also did "Weekend Update."

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.220
I did impressions with
Colin Quinn.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.788
And that was -- And then I got

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.423
all sorts of phone calls
and fun stuff.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.259
It was super-fun.
I'll never forget that.

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.961
That was awesome.
Thank you, Ben Stiller.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.230
We're going to talk about his
show, "Escape Room,"

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.766
that's airing
this Thursday on NBC

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:30.269
for Red Nose Day with him
and Jack Black

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.437
and Lisa Kudrow
and Courteney Cox.

00:04:32.437 --> 00:04:33.706
It's like a mini
"Friends" reunion.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.008
It's gonna be -- It's hilarious.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.610
And, also, we're going to
talk about his dad,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.678
who sadly passed away,
Jerry Stiller,

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:42.548
who, gosh, was so funny.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:45.217
I mean, but we're gonna talk to
Ben later in the show.

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:47.486
Then Hannah Gadsby,
speaking of funny.

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:49.389
We'll talk about her
new special, "Douglas",

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:54.293
that premieres May 26th
on Netflix.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:55.862
And then we're gonna
close out the show

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.663
with one of our
favorite musical guests.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.266
Tim McGraw will be here tonight.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.534
And it's super-fun.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.202
Oh, quickly,
I want to thank everyone

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.771
for voting for us for
the Webby Awards.

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:07.673
We won two Webbys.

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:10.108
So thank you very much
for voting.

00:05:10.108 --> 00:05:12.711
One was for writing for
the Amazon Alexa thing

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:14.212
that we did for
"Tell Me a Joke."

00:05:14.212 --> 00:05:15.848
And then the other is for

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:20.419
Best Celebrity or Fan
Social Media Content.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.588
That's maj. For the Webbys?
-That's amazing.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.224
-That's the one you want to win.
Thank you, guys, for voting.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:28.093
I love it, love it, love it.
It's awesome.

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:30.262
Hey, speaking of
fun things to do

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:33.265
with the web and the Internet,
what a segue this is.

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.835
Over the weekend, I talked to
my pal Steve Higgins,

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:38.304
my good friend, and he
showed me some Zoom hacks

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.371
that are really helpful.

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:40.706
Check it out.

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:43.075 line:0%
-Hey, Higgins. How's it going?
-Great. How about you?

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:45.678
-You know, hanging in there.
What have you been up to?

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:48.247
-Well, everybody's working
from home these days,

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:51.683
so I came up with some great
work-from-home hacks.

00:05:51.683 --> 00:05:54.987
First, I figured out some new
ways you can slack off

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.890
in a virtual meeting
by using Zoom backgrounds.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.159
-You can use Zoom backgrounds
to slack off?

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.061
How does that work?

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.563
-Like this. See?

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:06.899
That was a Zoom-video background
I made of myself, Jimmy.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.635
-You were a Zoom background
the whole time?

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.903
I had no idea.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.438
-Look at him.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:15.207
He has no clue
what we're talking about,

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:16.842
but it seems like he does.

00:06:16.842 --> 00:06:19.945
I can just plop this
into a work Zoom

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:22.981
and then I can spend my
time doing important things,

00:06:22.981 --> 00:06:24.951
like bonding with my kids

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:28.053
by screaming at them to
reorganize my Blu-rays.

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:29.689
-Show me another one.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:33.659
-This next hack requires
the help of a friend.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.095
And that friend is yourself.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:39.799
Hey, your car's on fire outside.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:43.603
Jimmy, his car [laughs]
isn't on fire.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.938
In fact, he doesn't even
have one.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.039
That's a Zoom video.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.841
And that's just a normal excuse

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.843
to get him out of
a cyber meeting.

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:54.814
-You were a Zoom background
that whole time? Wow.

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:57.616
-Wow.

00:06:57.616 --> 00:06:58.884
I've never seen
two of me before.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.919
I feel like I'm in one of
those beer commercials.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:03.589
"And twins."
More like "And me's."

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:04.856
-What else you got?

00:07:04.856 --> 00:07:07.793
Okay, for this next one...
Package!

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:10.229
Oh, shoot.
I guess the delivery man's here.

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:12.765
Can you hang on a second, Jimmy?

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.434
Yeah, delivery for...me?

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:18.704
Hey, "me"? That's my name.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:23.775
Yeah, but which one of us
is the real Higgins, Jimmy?

00:07:23.775 --> 00:07:25.944
Trick question.

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:28.247
They're both Zoom backgrounds.
I'm the real Higgins.

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:32.752
Jimmy, you don't -- you don't
seem impressed this time.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:38.256
That's because Jimmy was a
Zoom background the whole time.

00:07:38.256 --> 00:07:40.425
[ Gasps ]
Oh, my.

00:07:40.425 --> 00:07:43.528
Wow! Six Steve Higginses.

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:45.063
You know what that means.

00:07:45.063 --> 00:07:49.868
We could start our own Avengers
made up of six dads

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.503
with no superpowers,

00:07:51.503 --> 00:07:54.507
and one of them is deathly
allergic to peanuts.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:04.183
-Six Steve Higginses, everybody.
We'll be right back.

